        "original_id": "054c85b8-5f55-599f-aa04-14f4d5e39dbc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Osteomeles, Medinilla\n- Places: eastern Asia, Africa, Madagascar, southern Asia, western Pacific Ocean islands\n- Concepts: shrub traits, genus classification, species counts, native ranges\n\nFacts:\n- Osteomeles are shrubs native to eastern Asia.\n- Osteomeles have compound leaves, an opposite leaf arrangement, and small pome fruit.\n- Medinilla is a genus of about 193 species of flowering plants in the family Melastomataceae.\n- Medinilla is native to tropical regions of the Old World from Africa, which has two species, east through Madagascar, which has about 70 species, and southern Asia to the western Pacific Ocean islands.",
